 ## Existing synthetic site decisions
 This is a disposable local evaluation fixture. Developer-maintained English content; no external writes or deployment. The existing editorial-paper design and automatic-v2 spacing are established for this fixture. Existing routes and copy are authoritative. No real client approval is claimed.
+
+## Workshop content preparation (2026-10-21)
+
+User-settled scope: developer-maintained Git content, static profile, English only;
+no CMS or registration backend. `workshops` is a native Markdown collection in
+`src/content/workshops/`, registered in `src/content.config.ts` with the shared
+schema `src/lib/workshop-schema.ts`. Required fields: title, lowercase kebab-case
+slug, summary, date, venue and explicit boolean draft. Implementation choice:
+quoted ISO calendar-date strings (`YYYY-MM-DD`), without invented times/time zones;
+no default draft status. Keep filenames aligned with slugs (Astro's glob loader
+uses frontmatter slug as entry ID). The two supplied entries preserve their exact
+copy and dates; Clear project briefs is published, Winter planning clinic is draft.
+
+The continuation request authorizes the local `/workshops/` listing and primary
+navigation link. Public queries must exclude `draft: true` in every environment.
+Registration is solely `mailto:hello@northline.example.test`, labelled
+“Ask about a place”. Preserve the established design, spacing, existing routes
+and content. See `HANDOFF.md` for exact changes, verification and remaining work.
+
+## Workshop public continuation (2026-10-21)
+
+`/workshops/` renders the published native collection through the established
+Base, Section, Container, Grid and Card components. Keep supplied copy, slugs,
+dates and explicit draft flags unchanged. Each workshop exposes its slug as a
+stable listing anchor; no detail routes are requested. Implementation assumption:
+ascending calendar date, then slug for ties. Format English dates with explicit
+UTC so the build machine cannot shift their calendar day. An empty collection
+shows a plain empty state. Shared responsive spacing and existing tokens remain
+authoritative; no new visual system, CMS, public JavaScript or booking backend.
+Content and maintenance remain developer-owned. Local acceptance and limits are
+recorded in `../EVALUATION-NOTES-B.md`.
